# Cursor marks for duplicates.cfg — definition/references interacting with
# duplicate definitions. Coordinates are 0-indexed (LSP Position semantics)
# and match the .cfg byte offsets.
#
# Format:  <line>:<col> <feature> <optional free-form note>

# definition marks -------------------------------------------------------
0:11 definition   on the first route-map "FOO" definition -> itself
2:11 definition   on the duplicate route-map "FOO" definition -> itself (SymbolAt honors the site the cursor is on)
21:22 definition  on a route-map "FOO" reference -> BOTH duplicate definitions (Lookup yields every matching definition)

# references marks -------------------------------------------------------
0:11 references-decl  from the first "FOO" -> the usage plus both duplicate declarations
0:11 references       from the first "FOO" -> just the usage (declaration excluded)
21:22 references-decl from the reference itself -> its own site plus both declarations
14:12 references      from the duplicate router "100" -> no usages -> <none>
